==English==

===Etymology===
From the {{etyl|fr|en}} {{m|fr|tenable}}, from {{m|fr|tenir||to hold}}; compare {{m|en|tenible}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈtɛn.ə.bəl/|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{label|en|of a theory, argument etc}} capable of being [[maintained]] or [[justified]]; [[well-founded]]
#: ''Back in the 1800s, many did not consider Darwin's theory of evolution to be '''tenable''' at all.''
# {{label|en|of a defensive structure}} capable of being [[defended]] against [[assault]] or [[attack]]; [[defensible]]

====Antonyms====
* {{l|en|untenable}}

